<rtept lat="50.8317000000" lon="-0.7813300000">
<time>2026-05-28T08:26:09Z</time>
<name>Chichester Tramway Station</name>
<desc>The Chichester terminus of the Tramway stood on the far side of the Wiley building. It opened to acclaim on 27 August 1897. The Tramway was not connected to the main line except for transfer of rolling stock. The gasworks was across the road. Steam locomotives were originally used but railmotors were later introduced. The journey from here to Selsey was timetabled to take about 30 minutes but that proved to be very approximate on most occasions</desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
