<time>2026-05-28T08:26:09Z</time>
<name>Hoe Farm Halt</name>
<desc>The Tramway ran through what are now the two courses of Chichester Golf Club. Nothing can now be seen but there was a private farm halt here (last remains in photograph below) and a siding. In January 1915, two large elm trees fell on to the track during a severe gale but Miss Jupp of Hoe Farm was able to stop the train in time. Its passengers and crew were put up at the farmhouse until the line could be cleared. The delay was typical of the Tramway!</desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
<extensions>
<xstyle:fill>
<xstyle:color>ff0000</xstyle:color>
