</rtept>
<rtept lat="50.7601200000" lon="-0.7858000000">
<time>2026-05-28T08:26:09Z</time>
<name>Broad Rife Bridge</name>
<desc><![CDATA[This was the only fixed over bridge on the line, crossing from the embankment over Broad Rife which runs into Pagham Harbour. Rife is a Sussex word for a channel that drains water from agricultural land. 

The bridge was poorly built using harbour shingle in the concrete. It had to be rebuilt after the 1910 flood. 

The line continued a short distance from here to Ferry station.]]></desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
